  "vegetation": {
    "rule": "An instance is ON a deck if its XY falls inside a deck footprint AND the top of its own mesh bounding box rises above that deck top Z. That is exactly the set a frame can see standing in, poking through, or floating over the paving. An instance whose whole bounding box stays BELOW the deck top is buried under the platform, invisible in the state the deck exists in, and is NOT touched.",
    "ruleWhyNotEverythingInside": "Inside the precinct square the deck and the Modern city are opposites: AMikdashEnclosure hides the PrecinctCutOriginal terrain while the wall stands and hides the PrecinctCutTwin while the modern city stands, so the same ground is paved deck in the Yechezkel state and open hillside in the Modern state. Every plant inside that square is therefore correct in one state and wrong in the other. Removing only the ones that break the deck's surface keeps the Yechezkel frames clean at the smallest possible cost to the Modern hillside: the plants below the deck plane, which are the lower slopes, survive untouched.",
    "why": "release_vegetation.py ran on 9 Sep with keep-outs for the Mount enclosure ring and the architecture blocker boxes. BOTH plaza decks were built AFTER that scatter, so no keep-out covered them and the scatter planted straight through them.",
    "precedent": "release_vegetation.py already refuses instances that fall within existingTreeProximityCm of an existing tree (2,678 refused on the Candidate48 run). This is that same mechanism with a new primitive: a deck footprint instead of a tree radius.",
    "deckPriorityNote": "ORDER MATTERS AND A FIRST PASS GOT IT WRONG. The Kotel plaza stands inside the precinct rectangle in XY (X -23414..-14250, Y 11932..25000) but 10 to 12 m below it: the Kotel decks are at -1234.594 and -984.594 while the precinct deck is at 0. Tested against the precinct first, every plant on the Kotel plaza looked BURIED under the precinct deck and was kept - the dry run scored the Kotel 66 with the precinct absent and 0 with it present. The precinct deck does not actually cover the Kotel plaza: Scripts/create_kotel_opening.py cuts an opening for it, and in the Modern state AMikdashEnclosure hides the precinct plaza altogether and the Kotel plaza is the surface. So decks are tested in priority order, smallest and most specific first, and the first deck covering an instance's XY is the one it is judged against.",
    "deckPriorityOrder": [
      "kotel",
      "precinct"
    ],
