  "birds": {
    "why": "create_birds.py and release_birds.py both say so in their own honesty lists: NO MATERIAL IS CREATED OR ASSIGNED. All 20 bird meshes carry /Engine/EngineMaterials/WorldGridMaterial in both slots. WorldGridMaterial is DefaultLit and samples the tangent-space normal map T_Default_Material_Grid_N; the bird import logged degenerate tangent bases and nearly zero bi-normals on every species Level pose, so that normal map shades to garbage, and the placeholder planar UVs (measured span 0.03 to 0.19) put the whole bird inside a fraction of one grid cell, so there is no checker either. Uniformly dark, unshaded, bird-shaped-but-unreadable against a bright sky is exactly flat black quads.",
